e increases and that's a great way  to earn money coming in that you can use  to grow your business the last thing you  might want to consider is selling  subscriptions so I don't know how your  model works now but maybe they're buying  one month at a time or two months at a  time see if you could sell them for  longer so can you sell them for a season  so all the spring roll of summer or can  you sell them for the entire year and  you might give a little bit of a  discount to give them an incentive to  want to do that but the advantages you  get you  money upfront which can really help with  your cash flow and also give you the  money that you need to expand your  business so Kenosha I hope that helps  that's my thoughts on it I'm gonna turn  it over to a friend of mine Danny Indy  who has some thoughts as well and he's  gonna give you his advice  Rochelle thank you very much for your  email I get messages like this very  frequently from people who want to  expand their business or grow into a new  area or do upgrades or any number of  things that are gonna cost Mayan they're  wondering where they can go to get that  money and I always point them back to  the same place which is asking well why  don't they have the money already being  generated by their business you if you  mentioned in your in your message that  99 percent of the money that comes in  goes to pay your bills and to keep the  business running and so forth which  means that you aren't really making a  profit you aren't making extra money  that can be put aside and that's very  concerning to me it makes me wonder  what's gonna happen if there is an  emergency or something comes up or any  business needs to be making more money  than it costs to just keep everything  running and so my advice to you would be  to look at the way your business is  structured and find ways to improve your  profitability and at a very basic level  there's two ways of doing that you can  lower your costs or you can raise the